{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Except for his close relative.</b> It would appear to us that its meaning is like 'any man, to all his flesh relatives' — there he states a general category, and afterward specifies mother and father." "And the meaning of <b>a husband among his people</b> is that the husband shall not defile himself for his wife. But when we saw that our Sages rendered it 'he may defile himself for his wife,' and they brought as support 'for his close relative,' in the manner of an asmakhta, as I explained regarding the phrase לעם נכרי, and they said that 'husband' means a great one whose people are under his authority, like 'its master' — there is no nullification of the first interpretation. And the reason for mentioning the mother before the father is that the male lives longer than the female, in most cases."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "Resolved 'our Sages' (רבותינו) as referring to the rabbinic translators/interpreters of the verse; the phrase continues directly into a citation of their Aramaic rendering of 'בעל בעמיו יטמא לה' as 'יטמא לאשתו'."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:31.995362586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}